        <item>
    <title>Fleet 1.6.6</title>
    <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font: 13px -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif; line-height: 1.45; margin: 12px 16px; }
h2 { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; margin: 14px 0 4px; }
h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; }
li { margin: 3px 0; }
p { margin: 6px 0; }
code { font: 12px ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
</style>
<h2>New</h2><ul><li><b>Report a Problem.</b> If something looks wrong, like an agent that stays red after Claude finished, choose Help ▸ Report a Problem…, or right-click the agent. Fleet gathers what it saw at that moment, shows you all of it, and opens an email to us with it attached. Nothing is sent unless you send it, and it never includes your terminal, conversations or files.</li></ul><h2>Improved</h2><ul><li><b>The terminal selects like a normal one.</b> Drag to select, double-click a word, triple-click a line, ⌘C to copy. A single click still works in the program: it focuses a split pane or places Claude's cursor. Hold ⌥ to use Claude's own selection.</li></ul>]]></description>
